# WPNest — JavaScript Rules

## Aliases

```text
@js  → sources/js/
@css → sources/css/
```

> Note: The `@scss` alias has been removed. The project uses `sources/css/` (Tailwind v4).

## Entry Pattern

- **Eager imports** → Global UI only (menu, navigation).
- **Lazy imports** → Use `import()` with a DOM check.

```js
import deviceMenu from '@js/common/deviceMenu.js';
deviceMenu();

if (document.querySelector('.home-slider')) {
	import('@js/common/swiperInit.js').then(({ initHomeSlider }) => initHomeSlider());
}
```

## Tailwind & JS Interaction

- Toggle Tailwind classes via `classList.add()` / `classList.remove()` / `classList.toggle()`.
- JS-driven state classes (`.is-open`, `.is-clicked`) are styled in `sources/css/menu.css` — not via Tailwind utilities — because they require pseudo-element or complex state CSS.
- Never write inline `element.style.*` for layout/color — add or remove Tailwind classes instead.

## Modules

- One file = one feature.
- Use named exports.
- Keep DOM logic inside `init()`.

## Standards

- Use `const` / `let` only.
- Never use `var`.
- No inline `<script>` in PHP.
- New module → lazy-load from `script.js`.
- AJAX → `sources/js/modules/ajax-scripts.js`.
